{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_01a06e2295b37310acdda925c91d2565","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"powder list --mine \"$POWDER_AGENT\" --repo misty-step/canopy 2>&1; echo \"EXIT:$?\"; echo \"===TAKEABLE===\"; powder list --takeable --repo misty-step/canopy 2>&1; echo \"EXIT:$?\""},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-critic-discovery-id-collision\",\n    \"title\": \"Discovery ID collisions silently drop discoverable Forest instances\",\n    \"spec\": \"Problem: discovery deduplicates roots but generates IDs with sanitizeID; names such as agent_test and agent-test both become agent-test. Reconciliation keys workers/state by ID, so distinct roots can silently collapse or swap targets across scans.\\n\\nOutcome: discovered instances with distinct normalized roots must not silently share an effective identity. Resolve collisions deterministically before worker/state reconciliation, preserving stable route-to-root binding across repeated scans and input order changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and existing explicit inventory preservation tests. Exercise fleet selection for each resolved instance. Correct original draft example: agent_test and agent-beta do not collide; agent_test and agent-test do.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:56:11.467Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:56.828Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788550542915580458-critic, git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: discovery.go:16 keys discovered candidates by root path, so DiscoverLocalInstances can return multiple instances whose sanitized IDs collide: sanitizeID (discovery.go:196-210) maps \\\"agent_test\\\" and \\\"agent-beta\\\" style names to the same ID (both \\\"agent-test\\\", underscores and dashes both normalize to \\\"-\\\"). app.go:239-241 then builds discMap keyed by instance ID, so the second colliding instance silently overwrites the first in the map and, at app.go:275-283, is skipped via existingMap — a working Forest checkout simply never appears in the fleet, with no log or error. The same silent-drop applies if a discovered ID matches an explicit inventory ID.\\nRequired: every discoverable, validated instance must either appear in the fleet or its omission must be surfaced; discovery IDs must be unique per instance or collisions must be resolved deterministically and observably.\\nProposed spec direction: make DiscoverLocalInstances deduplicate or disambiguate by ID (e.g. suffix the ID from the root path on collision) before returning, or make syncDiscoveredInstances log/record dropped collisions; add a discovery test with two sibling dirs whose names sanitize to the same ID.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:56:11.467Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:31:56.483Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Blocking executive review of exact revision 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267; two independent reproductions run in an isolated git-archive checkout against actual source, go test -run TestExecutive -count=1 . exited 1. (1) syncDiscoveredInstances with A={ID:x,Root:/tmp/a} and B={ID:x,Root:/tmp/b}, then a scan containing only B: surviving route changes x-2 -\\u003e x. Counter assignment is topology-dependent; rebuilding it each scan breaks route-to-root stability and can retain the old x worker/state under a different root. Preserve existing discovered endpoint identity during reconciliation, then allocate only new identities; test removal, addition, and reappearance, not just reversed simultaneous inputs. (2) resolveDiscoveryCollisions with local Root=/srv/forest and explicit Host=other.example,Root=/srv/forest returns zero discovered entries. explicitRoots is keyed only by path, so an unrelated SSH target hides the local checkout. Include transport/host in endpoint equality; only an explicit local entry for the same local root may suppress its discovery. Tests added on the branch cover same-host duplicates and fixed-set reordering but neither failing transition. Both failures reproduced in 0.002s; no source changes applied to branch, no Gate verdict fabricated. Required correction belongs to this existing job. Also remove tests pinning -2 counter allocation rather than the stable-identity contract.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Problem: discovery deduplicates roots but generates IDs with sanitizeID; names such as agent_test and agent-test both become agent-test. Reconciliation keys workers/state by ID, so distinct roots can silently collapse or swap targets across scans.\\n\\nOutcome: discovered instances with distinct normalized roots must not silently share an effective identity. Resolve collisions deterministically before worker/state reconciliation, preserving stable route-to-root binding across repeated scans and input order changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and existing explicit inventory preservation tests. Exercise fleet selection for each resolved instance. Correct original draft example: agent_test and agent-beta do not collide; agent_test and agent-test do.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.665Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:31:56.483Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-publication-primary-refresh\",\n    \"title\": \"Preserve pre-publication primary refresh in Builder and Fixer policy\",\n    \"spec\": \"Make the proven local pre-publication primary-refresh policy durable through a normal exact-revision review request. Scope only agents/builder/agent.md and agents/fixer/agent.md (or their established shared owner if current primary already centralizes this policy). Build from current origin primary; do not copy dirty main-checkout files wholesale or import unrelated operational edits.\\n\\nBefore preparing review-request payloads, both roles must fetch origin and require the final checked revision to contain origin/${FOREST_PRIMARY_REF#refs/heads/}. If stale, rebase their subject/repair onto the fetched primary, preserve both feature and primary behavior, and rerun every configured check before publishing the resulting SHA. Failed rebase/check stops publication. Fixer must retain the original rejected SHA for Kernel compare-and-swap. Preserve Kernel atomic publication and the Verifier/Gate ancestry check: this guard reduces avoidable stale publication but cannot eliminate later races. Add no scheduler, retry loop, dependency, new role, or Kernel code.\\n\\nEvidence: collision revision 34b04b06de58ebfe735dedd977b00c2a614cc752 passed checks but was stale because 73d1489 landed during implementation. Local Fixer policy digest 4d7e25ef73d3dad94e08d461a7347a6c4cde500e195c81bd3d60d4c547671c32 was exercised by Run 1788552644310643252-fixer: it refetched, verified ancestry, and published 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267 with original rejected-SHA CAS.\\n\\nAcceptance: reviewable minimal role-policy diff on current primary; supported forest declaration show loads both declarations without errors; repository checks pass; exact request/verdict/Gate evidence integrates the policy. Do not add source-text tests for prompts or claim local runtime hashes prove Git integration.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-05T00:21:29.67Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:17:54.108Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Execution prerequisite observed after promotion: Canopy Verifier Run 1788552943774438475-verifier failed on OpenRouter 402 for a 384000-token output reservation, before publishing any verdict. Shared root-cause job is misty-step/iron-forest:if-provider-output-ceiling. This is not a code/check rejection and does not invalidate prior exact approvals. Keep this job takeable for Builder implementation; integration needs a successful provider-backed Verifier Run. Do not change transport credentials or bypass Gate to complete it.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:21:29.67Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:28:25.63Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"Post-publication integration diagnosis: real service-environment forest poll verifier returns 0 (ready), while supported trigger show verifier reports run_error=\\\"provider budget exhausted\\\" and no active Run. Kernel service is active. Thus the pending eebc1cc9968e3eb37715549d78fc9d0a233553a1 review is not stranded by Powder scope or lack of request work; provider admission is the current hold. Do not reset/bypass the guard without fixing admission. Shared output-ceiling job remains unclaimed at the last read.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:16:08.947Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:16:08.947Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Make the proven local pre-publication primary-refresh policy durable through a normal exact-revision review request. Scope only agents/builder/agent.md and agents/fixer/agent.md (or their established shared owner if current primary already centralizes this policy). Build from current origin primary; do not copy dirty main-checkout files wholesale or import unrelated operational edits.\\n\\nBefore preparing review-request payloads, both roles must fetch origin and require the final checked revision to contain origin/${FOREST_PRIMARY_REF#refs/heads/}. If stale, rebase their subject/repair onto the fetched primary, preserve both feature and primary behavior, and rerun every configured check before publishing the resulting SHA. Failed rebase/check stops publication. Fixer must retain the original rejected SHA for Kernel compare-and-swap. Preserve Kernel atomic publication and the Verifier/Gate ancestry check: this guard reduces avoidable stale publication but cannot eliminate later races. Add no scheduler, retry loop, dependency, new role, or Kernel code.\\n\\nEvidence: collision revision 34b04b06de58ebfe735dedd977b00c2a614cc752 passed checks but was stale because 73d1489 landed during implementation. Local Fixer policy digest 4d7e25ef73d3dad94e08d461a7347a6c4cde500e195c81bd3d60d4c547671c32 was exercised by Run 1788552644310643252-fixer: it refetched, verified ancestry, and published 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267 with original rejected-SHA CAS.\\n\\nAcceptance: reviewable minimal role-policy diff on current primary; supported forest declaration show loads both declarations without errors; repository checks pass; exact request/verdict/Gate evidence integrates the policy. Do not add source-text tests for prompts or claim local runtime hashes prove Git integration.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:16:08.947Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:28:25.63Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  }\n]\n"}],"details":{}}}
