50cmlidXRvci0yMDI2MDkwMnxtZXRhIn0\",\"format\":\"meta-responses-v1\",\"id\":\"rs_6a9b2bb9928e46ac7ab744e0:rs_01a06e22d3aa7250827e1aa41f7e20d1\",\"index\":1}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01a06e22d4737582b1d7f337137b50ae","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788554148540142854-builder/agents/_shared/skills/powder/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor","usage":{"input":400,"output":312,"cacheRead":10737,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":201,"totalTokens":11449,"cost":{"input":0.00037999999999999997,"output":0.001248,"cacheRead":0.00171792,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0033459199999999996}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788554168935,"responseId":"gen-1788554169-HLtQoM6OcRrqqCITn6ga","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a06e22d4737582b1d7f337137b50ae","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: powder\ndescription: >\n  Powder is the exclusive-work ledger. Use when listing takeable jobs\n  for this repository, taking a job, asking the operator, or completing\n  work with proof after an approve Gate.\n---\n\n# Powder\n\nPowder stores jobs. Take one. Finish it. Write proof.\n\n## Client contract\n\nOrigin resolves from `POWDER_URL`, then `~/.config/powder/config`; there is no\ndefault. Remote origins require HTTPS; HTTP is loopback-only. `POWDER_AGENT` is\noptional audit metadata. Managed workers pass the\nexact canonical label `forest-misty-step/powder`, but this label never\nauthorizes a lease or any other operation. `POWDER_API_KEY` is transport\nauthentication.\n\nRun `powder doctor [--agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"]` before selection to verify the\nconfigured origin and service. If the check fails, do not call Powder. GitHub\nIssues remain the Tracker.\n\nEach successful `powder take` returns a flat JSON Job plus a per-job\n`claim_token` made from 32 random bytes encoded as base64url. Only its SHA-256\nhash is stored in `jobs.lease_token_hash`. A live job returns `held` unless\nthe CLI presents that job's matching stored claim, which resumes it. An audit\nlabel never grants resume. The claim token is capability for only that lease.\n\nThe CLI stores claim tokens privately under XDG state by validated origin and\njob id, resumes by job id, and sends them automatically. It never prints\nclaims, and list/show/logs/notes never expose them. `release`, `renew`, `ask`,\n`done`, live-job field edits, and live `abandon` require the claim; missing is\n`claim_required`, and mismatch or expiry is `invalid_claim`. `note` stays\nreport-authorized and claim-independent. Free-job patching or abandon uses\n`promote` authority without a claim. Tokens are deleted after release, ask,\ndone, or abandon.\n\n## Factory loop\n\n1. When `POWDER_AGENT` is set, run\n   `powder list --mine \"$POWDER_AGENT\" --repo <forest.yaml repo>`. Treat\n   `--mine` as an audit-label filter, never as resumable authority. A live\n   candidate is resumable only when `powder take <id> [--agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"]`\n   succeeds with the private claim stored for this origin and job id, and no\n   `forest/<id>/*` branch exists. When `POWDER_AGENT` is unset, attempt\n   resumption only for a job id supplied by the managed run or current branch;\n   otherwise continue to takeable selection.\n2. `powder list --takeable --repo <forest.yaml repo>`\n3. `powder show <id>`\n   The spec is the work. Empty spec is not takeable. Show never contains a\n   claim token.\n4. `powder take <id> [--agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"]`\n   Do this before creating a branch. A successful take stores the private\n   claim. A live job returns `held`, even under the same audit label; do not\n   interpret `held` as permission from the label. Keep a published Subject\n   held for the Kernel completion loop, and release only a failed or\n   unpublished Builder attempt.\n5. A Fixer uses the same Subject's private claim by job id before branch\n   mutation; the audit label is only metadata.\n6. Publish with schema v2, `tracker` set to the source actually selected\n   (`github` or `powder`), and branch `forest/<id>/<slug>`. Every Subject uses\n   that shape, including GitHub Issue numbers.\n7. Agents do not call `powder done`. The Kernel completes the current\n   Git-landed Subject only when request evidence has `tracker: powder`, using\n   the approved Revision as proof. The CLI clears the private claim after\n   completion or any release/ask/abandon.\n\nMultiple distinct jobs may be held under the same managed audit label. Every\nclaim authorizes only its own job; managed workers and the Kernel do not mint\nor share authority from the label.\n\n\n## Verbs\n\n```\npowder list --takeable --repo REPO\npowder list --mine AGENT --repo REPO\npowder show ID\npowder take ID\npowder release ID\npowder ask ID --question '...'\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788554171909},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01a06e22d7fd7e03813038e974f09122","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"powder show canopy-verifier-current-subject 2>&1; echo \"EXIT:$?\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor","usage":{"input":1286,"output":63,"cacheRead":11121,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12470,"cost":{"input":0.0012216999999999998,"output":0.000252,"cacheRead":0.00177936,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00325306}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788554171910,"responseId":"gen-1788554171-z1ERsRh4tBsmUTZkM3t1","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a06e22d7fd7e03813038e974f09122","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"canopy-verifier-current-subject\",\n  \"title\": \"Read current Powder contract and review evidence before verdict publication\",\n  \"spec\": \"Make current Subject feedback an explicit read-only Verifier input in agents/verifier/agent.md. For request tracker=powder, read powder show \\u003csubject\\u003e before reviewing and again immediately before publishing a verdict; require matching repository, current spec, and notes. Reconcile conflicting instructions or reproductions explicitly against behavior rather than silently ignoring or blindly accepting them. If the current Subject contract cannot be read, do not approve. Do not acquire, release, or complete its claim. Preserve exact-revision request provenance, configured checks, and Gate ancestry requirements; GitHub requests must not invoke Powder.\\n\\nReason: the pending collision revision 3af7c062e632f0677f6ef4db399188ffd8484267 has two experimentally reproduced blockers added after publication (route reassignment on disappearance; remote path suppresses local discovery). The local Verifier declaration previously only said available actionable review feedback without naming how to obtain current Powder notes. Local operational change already loads as digest 97d73b32c0d5abeba4daf78670218f651bbfb9960c710c0c4dfbefd0a8e7b9d5; make only this policy durable from current primary, without copying unrelated dirty main-checkout changes.\\n\\nProof: declaration show accepts the changed Verifier policy; configured checks pass; normal exact-revision review request and Gate integrate it. No source-text tests for prompts. In subsequent real review, retain evidence of read-only current Subject lookup and disposition of actionable notes. Keep policy-only change small; no new state, tools, credentials, or Kernel mechanisms.\",\n  \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"lease\": null,\n  \"ask\": null,\n  \"proof\": null,\n  \"abandoned\": false,\n  \"notes\": [],\n  \"created_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T20:33:20.929Z\",\n  \"promotions\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T20:33:20.929Z\",\n      \"by\": \"none\",\n      \"spec\": \"Make current Subject feedback an explicit read-only Verifier input in agents/verifier/age