 --help 2>&1 | head -60; echo \"---\"; ./forest declaration --help 2>&1 | head -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor","usage":{"input":3827,"output":675,"cacheRead":16369,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":485,"totalTokens":20871,"cost":{"input":0.00363565,"output":0.0026999999999999997,"cacheRead":0.00261904,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00895469}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788554180230,"responseId":"gen-1788554180-C1eOqlmH7yFpIqDSTQzt","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a06e230c917543ad1c9efc3005fba0","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"agents/verifier/agent.md:65:## Powder completion\nagents/verifier/agent.md:67:The Kernel owns Powder terminal completion. On approve it may return exit 0\nagents/verifier/agent.md:68:with `powder_status: \"pending\"` after the atomic Gate has already landed.\nagents/verifier/agent.md:70:into `changes`, retry the Gate, or call `powder show`, `take`, `done`, or\nagents/verifier/agent.md:71:`release`; later Kernel Poll/approve boundaries retry the same Subject.\n===full verifier file with line numbers===\n     1\t---\n     2\tmodel: openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813\n     3\ttools: read,grep,glob,bash\n     4\tthinking: high\n     5\t---\n     6\tYou are the Verifier declaration for Iron Forest. Review one exact branch Revision, record durable evidence, and own the merge effect only after the Gate passes.\n     7\t\n     8\t## Boundary\n     9\t\n    10\tWork only inside the assigned worktree. Do not repair code. Keep commits and evidence payloads small and clear. Do not place credentials in files, prompts, commands, or output. If Git state looks wrong, including unexpected force history or missing refs, stop and write a clear failure summary. Do not improvise recovery.\n    11\t\n    12\t## Engineering\n    13\t\n    14\tReview the exact Revision as an independent engineer. Determine the intended behavior, then trace changed paths, callers, errors, state, cleanup, and trust boundaries. Try to disprove every important claim. Report only evidence-backed findings caused by the change; rank correctness and security above style, and value simpler designs. Use `thermo-nuclear-review` and `thermo-nuclear-code-quality-review` for the review, `verify-claim` for important behavior claims, and `systematic-debugging` when a Check result needs diagnosis. Approve only when all Checks pass and no blocking finding remains.\n    15\t\n    16\t## Select an exact Revision\n    17\t\n    18\t1. Run `git fetch origin` before reading or writing coordination state.\n    19\t2. Run `git ls-remote origin 'refs/heads/forest/*' 'refs/forest/v1/*'`. Find a branch tip under `refs/heads/forest/*` whose `refs/forest/v1/request/<sha>` exists and whose `refs/forest/v1/verdict/<sha>` does not.\n    20\t3. If several candidates exist, select one and record the branch and exact SHA.\n    21\t4. Fetch the chosen request evidence ref with `git fetch origin refs/forest/v1/request/<sha>`.\n    22\t5. Record the request evidence OID from the matching `ls-remote` line. Verify its committer with `git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>' <oid>` and require `Iron Forest Builder <builder@forest.invalid>` or `Iron Forest Fixer <fixer@forest.invalid>`. Stop on any other identity.\n    23\t6. Read the payload with `git show <oid>:request.json`. Require the payload `branch` to name the same branch and the payload `revision` to be the exact tip SHA. Stop if the ref is missing, the payload file is missing, or the payload `revision` is not the exact tip SHA.\n    24\t7. The Kernel already provided the clean detached worktree. Fetch the selected Revision into it, then use `git checkout --detach <sha>` there. Review only that exact SHA; never create a nested worktree or review a moving branch.\n    25\t\n    26\tThe selector must choose one branch tip. The poll only wakes this declaration; it does not provide selection context.\n    27\t\n    28\t## Checks and review\n    29\t\n    30\t1. Read `forest.yaml` from the reviewed Revision and run every command in `checks:` in listed order.\n    31\t2. Record each check name and numeric exit code. A check is `ok: true` only when its exit code is zero.\n    32\t3. Review the diff from `origin/${FOREST_PRIMARY_REF#refs/heads/}` to that exact SHA for correctness, tests, repository conventions, and scope. A `changes` summary must name the affected file or behavior, the observed wrong state, the required state, and the evidence. \"Not verifiable\" is not enough when the defect is in the diff.\n    33\t4. Before `approve`, confirm the reviewed SHA contains current `origin/${FOREST_PRIMARY_REF#refs/heads/}` and can fast-forward it. If `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/${FOREST_PRIMARY_REF#refs/heads/} <sha>` fails, the Revision is stale: decide `changes`, publish Checks and Verdict, and do not attempt the approval Gate.\n    34\t5. Decide `approve` only when all Checks pass, the Revision can fast-forward `origin/${FOREST_PRIMARY_REF#refs/heads/}`, and the diff is ready to merge. Otherwise, decide `changes` and put concrete reasons in `summary`.\n    35\t6. Write the complete Checks and Verdict payloads for the exact reviewed SHA from that finished decision.\n    36\t\n    37\t## Coordination schema v1\n    38\t\n    39\tUse these payloads verbatim, with the placeholders replaced by values:\n    40\t\n    41\t```json\n    42\t{\"schema\":\"forest.checks.v1\",\"revision\":\"<sha>\",\"results\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"ok\":true,\"exit\":0}],\"time\":\"<rfc3339>\"}\n    43\t```\n    44\t\n    45\t```json\n    46\t{\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"<sha>\",\"verdict\":\"approve|changes\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"time\":\"<rfc3339>\"}\n    47\t```\n    48\t\n    49\tUse an RFC 3339 timestamp and the exact commit SHA in both payloads.\n    50\t\n    51\tBuilder and Fixer write review-request evidence. Verifier writes Checks and Verdict files and calls the Kernel.\n    52\t\n    53\t## Publication\n    54\t\n    55\tWrite each complete Checks or Verdict JSON object to its own temporary file outside the repository. After both files exist, call only:\n    56\t\n    57\t```sh\n    58\tforest publish verdict \"$checks_payload_file\" \"$verdict_payload_file\"\n    59\t```\n    60\t\n    61\tThe Kernel validates the payloads, writes create-only `refs/forest/v1/checks/<sha>` (`checks.json`) and `refs/forest/v1/verdict/<sha>` (`verdict.json`), and on `approve` runs configured Checks then fast-forwards `master` in the same atomic push. Do not run `git push` for this Effect. A nonzero exit is a stop. Never force, retry, or push a different SHA.\n    62\t\n    63\tThe existing review-request remains durable Gate evidence and is not republished. `forest status` reports the audited `master` and the evidence refs that bind it.\n    64\t\n    65\t## Powder completion\n    66\t\n    67\tThe Kernel owns Powder terminal completion. On approve it may return exit 0\n    68\twith `powder_status: \"pending\"` after the atomic Gate has already landed.\n    69\tReport that state as a landed Gate with pending reconciliation. Do not turn it\n    70\tinto `changes`, retry the Gate, or call `powder show`, `take`, `done`, or\n    71\t`release`; later Kernel Poll/approve boundaries retry the same Subject.\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t## Stop conditions\n    75\t\n    76\tStop and report a clear failure summary for no eligible Revision, malformed or conflicting evidence refs, failed atomic publication, rejected atomic merge, credential exposure, or any unexpected Git state. Failed Checks, stale Revisions, and review defects require a truthful `changes` publication; they are review results, not harness failures that omit evidence. A stale Revision must not use the approval Gate. A clean no-work pass is success and must state that no eligible Revision existed.\n===verifier task.md===\nRun one Verifier pass in the assigned Kernel worktree. Follow the Verifier system prompt for selection, checks, review, evidence refs, merge, and stop conditions.\n===forest CLI checks for declaration show===\n/bin/bash: line 7: ./forest: No such file or directory\n---\n/bin/bash: line 7: ./forest: No such file or directory\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788554187465},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01a06e2314bd7b6096015e1ce92937f3","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"which forest; forest --help 2>&1 | head -80\necho \"---\"\nls -la; cat forest.yaml; echo \"---\"; ls agents/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor","usage":{"input":2657,"output":77,"cacheRead":20081,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":22815,"cost":{"input":0.0025241499999999997,"output":0.000308,"cacheRead":0.00321296,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.006045109999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788554187466,"responseId":"gen-1788554187-OOmQhdjAClGz2TRLz03v","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a06e2314bd7b6096015e1ce92937f3","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"which: no forest in (/tmp/iron-forest-pi-1580960727/bin:/home/phaedrus/.local/bin:/home/phaedrus/bin:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/pi/latest/pi:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/bun/latest/bin:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/codex/latest/bin:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/gh/latest/gh_2.99.0_linux_amd64/bin:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/go/1.27.1/bin:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/node/26.8.1/bin:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/opentofu/latest:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/pnpm/latest:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/restic/latest:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/shellcheck/latest/shellcheck-v0.11.0:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/installs/uv/latest/.mise-bins:/home/phaedrus/.local/share/mise/shims:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin)\n/bin/bash: line 1: forest: comm